      "content": "hey, i need some advice on something pretty sensitive. i've been working on some foundational code for a major Layer 1 protocol (the one everyone thinks was built by [REDACTED] and their VC backers) but i've kept my identity completely decoupled from the repo for security reasons. \n\nproblem is, the \"devs\" they have on the front are starting to claim all the credit and i'm tired of being the ghost in the machine. i want to leak enough cryptographic proof to show i'm the actual architect without getting doxxed or hunted by the firms that are currently managing the protocol. how can i prove authorship of the core logic without exposing my actual identity/IP?",
